@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple BPMN choreography — 2-3 banded tasks, sequence flow, no enclosing pool.
'   usecase:      Teach choreography task, participant banding (initiator white, responder grey), no pools.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       business-process
' ============================================================================
title Example BPMN Choreography - Simple Handshake

' BPMN choreography has NO enclosing pool. Each task is a banded rectangle:
'   - top band   = initiating participant (white)
'   - bottom band= responding participant (shaded)
' Inside the task: the message(s) exchanged (one-way or two-way).
' PlantUML has no native choreography shape; we model bands using
' nested rectangles and a `package` per task.

' --- Start / End events (thin / thick circles) ----------------------------
usecase " " as Start
usecase " " as End1

' --- Choreography tasks (banded) -----------------------------------------
package "Request Greeting\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as CT1 {
}
package "Return Quote\n[ Seller | Buyer ]" as CT2 {
}
package "Confirm Order\n[ Buyer | Seller ]" as CT3 {
}

Start --> CT1
CT1 --> CT2
CT2 --> CT3
CT3 --> End1

note top of CT1
  <b>Choreography task</b>
  Top band (white)  = <b>Buyer</b> (initiator)
  Bottom band (grey)= <b>Seller</b> (responder)
  Task carries the message(s):
  Buyer -> Seller : "Hello"
end note

note right of CT2
  Roles swap:
  Seller initiates the
  return quote, Buyer responds.
end note

note bottom of Start
  <b>Key difference</b>
  No enclosing pool. The
  choreography IS the
  collaboration's protocol.
end note

@enduml
